            <ArticleTitle>[Coronary heart disease; surgical aspects (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1531-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aspects of indication, of the surgical technique as well as long-term results are discussed on the basis of own experiences in 279 coronary artery operations. Patients suffering from unstable angina pectoris should be operated on as soon as possible. In cases with stable angina pectoris due to a triple vessel disease the long-term results are better with surgery than without.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
